[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29b3c018-edde-524b-b06c-f153e53c6290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526171} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe3c20f-e840-5440-be2a-f5c1a1149fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526179} {:answer/id #uuid "8d818a12-395f-5c83-b461-dd04476ca3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526194} {:answer/id #uuid "97dc724b-fd0c-5de0-a119-9a708a167c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526196} {:answer/id #uuid "fd87050e-7f2f-5d31-83ca-382f859c360b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d818a12-395f-5c83-b461-dd04476ca3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526194} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38fe45d-dbbd-5614-9a2b-4a1fd9aeb2c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "426d8119-038e-5752-a27b-06550594a590" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y)=- x^{2} y - x y^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $g(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=- 2 x y - y^{2},\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=- x^{2} - 2 x y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =- r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =- 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =(- r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0280772c-4d86-54c4-9ab1-42cbec9f9517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526157} {:answer/id #uuid "9306357a-dd3a-55a8-86f4-13d69d861185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526195} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1045dc-ae7b-53d6-a201-09fd8a333326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526198} {:answer/id #uuid "ab089900-ab5c-58c7-b4fc-284ea3c05606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526203} {:answer/id #uuid "e746cd53-7432-5738-9ad8-542080a2827e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9306357a-dd3a-55a8-86f4-13d69d861185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526195} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dd9e72c-be44-595b-952d-4e4727b9d32d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8479fa83-fbbd-5793-b8d0-0b7149751139" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=- 2 x^{2} y + 3 x y^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=- 4 x y + 3 y^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 2 x^{2} + 6 x y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta} & =(3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4b70f1-a2a9-50cf-83a8-2af7e51db9b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 14 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526165} {:answer/id #uuid "25451830-b3c4-5ed7-907b-8021140d7082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526168} {:answer/id #uuid "80d2b349-1aa9-5707-a1f3-27d64fedfcb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 14 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526189} {:answer/id #uuid "88268ae5-df7c-5cd6-b910-e71adbf29cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526191} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5b502e-7cdc-57c8-818e-2a9249e80994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 14 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce5b502e-7cdc-57c8-818e-2a9249e80994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 14 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526214} :answer-field/id #uuid "cea47898-ec2b-520f-a44f-e17d98f48686" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8945f7df-fee5-566f-aa38-1a5d974cb343" :question/problem "Given that $w(x,y)=4 x^{2} - x y - 3 y^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $w(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂w}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂w}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂w}{∂x}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂w}{∂y}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x}=8 x - y,\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y}=- x - 6 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =- 6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta} & =(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 14 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "282f6b6d-7109-520e-aba8-fa9ab8b0a7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526170} {:answer/id #uuid "3391d5eb-68ff-5f47-8cb4-841e008f9b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526173} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d504c1-fe78-5a56-8d10-4e6193ffaa1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526202} {:answer/id #uuid "e346e4b3-24c9-5ab1-b792-11794c240dfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526218} {:answer/id #uuid "e860279b-77dd-57ba-a0d7-ecb00ace3f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4d504c1-fe78-5a56-8d10-4e6193ffaa1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526202} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d102c59-1b9a-5a50-a344-4599186d21a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ba2b920-eb38-5aa2-a748-ae3fcff5a4ef" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=- 2 x^{2} + 3 x y + 4 y^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂r},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂r}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂r} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\right)(\\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\right)(\\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=- 4 x + 3 y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3 x + 8 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =8 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r} & =(3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(8 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0713a1ad-ccc7-566c-8914-8e3c100172f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526159} {:answer/id #uuid "16e60cd4-3e70-5728-807b-4b3fe56363b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526160} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb1511f-fd6f-5dcb-a549-16c1fa181fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526183} {:answer/id #uuid "6f531e11-04da-524b-a34c-49484bbe1b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526184} {:answer/id #uuid "b677097d-e76f-536a-ba5b-84dc2520444d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bb1511f-fd6f-5dcb-a549-16c1fa181fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526183} :answer-field/id #uuid "178906e3-57c0-56b7-986d-f2501a1f24d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b47877ef-eea0-5bca-bfa7-432b3e6a60d6" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 3 x y + y^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $g(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=8 x + 3 y,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=3 x + 2 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =(3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(- 3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =- 3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fcac3a0-3569-5248-9a48-274baa2fe77a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526172} {:answer/id #uuid "b06fe44e-a0ff-5fe5-95fa-c4dddd61fddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526204} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d022e8-17ef-5195-8caa-81e89fedfa62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526211} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b74784-ec66-503f-a057-72a84744d3ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\